# The game machine's front door: port 80 to the composed host on 4000.
#
#   caddy validate --config Caddyfile     # after any edit
#   caddy run --config Caddyfile          # foreground, for trying it
#   brew services start caddy             # as a service; caddy reads
#                                         # /opt/homebrew/etc/Caddyfile, so
#                                         # symlink this file there:
#                                         #   ln -sf ~/Developer/game-host/Caddyfile \
#                                         #          /opt/homebrew/etc/Caddyfile
#
# This file used to route a path prefix per game to a port per game, plus a
# menu root and three bare-prefix redirects — nine blocks whose only job was
# knowing the names of three games. One process serves all of them now
# (apps/host, port 4000 per PORTS.md), including the menu at `/` and each
# game's prefix below it, so none of that knowledge belongs out here any more.
#
# What that buys, and the reason the collapse is the point rather than a
# tidy-up: **adding a game is no longer a Caddyfile edit.** It is a row in
# apps/host/host.ts. This file cannot go stale against the game list because it
# no longer has one.
#
# Still true, and still load-bearing: the path is never stripped. Each game's
# client is *built* under its own base path — Rail Baron's basePath.ts says
# '/railbaron' — so assets are requested at `<base>/assets/…` and nothing
# rewrites them. A plain `reverse_proxy` passes the path through untouched,
# which is exactly what the games expect. If a rewrite or a `handle_path` ever
# appears here, that is the bug.
#
# Sockets need nothing special: every game mounts socket.io under its own base
# path (specs/2026-08-17-origin-relative-clients.md, implemented 2026-08-18),
# so they ride this one proxy like any other request. Caddy proxies WebSocket
# upgrades natively.
#
# Retired with the menu block: the `{env.HOME}` warning that used to live here.
# Homebrew's caddy service overrides HOME to its own storage dir, so that
# placeholder worked under `caddy run` and silently 404'd as a service (found
# the hard way 2026-08-17). No path in this file needs HOME any more — but the
# /opt/homebrew/etc/game-host symlink that lesson produced is still doing the
# same job for launchd/com.game-host.plist, so do not remove it.

# Any name this machine answers to on the LAN. `.local` covers the mDNS name
# through renames; add a real domain here if subdomain routing ever lands.
http:// {
	reverse_proxy localhost:4000
}
